# FreeLand

# --- Never commit: other people's drawings and correspondence ---------------
# user_help/ holds files sent to us by users seeking support, plus draft
# replies to them. Those files are theirs, not ours, and their names are in
# them. They are kept here because that is where the work happens; they must
# not reach github.com/hawstom/freeland.
#
# This rule is adequate, not a lock. `git add -f` still overrides it, and it
# does nothing about zips or backups of the working tree.
Turning_Path_Tracker/user_help/

# --- Never commit: the website working copy --------------------------------
# hawsedc.com/ is a clone of github.com/hawstom/hawsedc.com, nested here for
# convenience because TURN's released files live in its gnu/ directory. It has
# its own history and its own remote. Without this rule git offers to commit it
# as a gitlink, which would be wrong in both repos.
Turning_Path_Tracker/hawsedc.com/

# --- Build and test output -------------------------------------------------
# Produced by a run, not authored. Regenerate it; do not track it.
Turning_Path_Tracker/devtools/turn-integration-out.dwg
Turning_Path_Tracker/devtools/turn-curve-out.dwg
Turning_Path_Tracker/devtools/turn-punch-out.dwg
Turning_Path_Tracker/devtools/turn-tests-out.dwg
# Written by tt-safe-quit so QUIT has nothing to ask about. See CLAUDE.md.
Turning_Path_Tracker/devtools/turn-scratch.dwg

